	(text "[■] POINT 12: TH1 THERMISTOR DNP ASSIGNMENT\n    • Set TH1 attribute to DNP (Do Not Populate) in the schematic.\n    • Verify TH1 is completely excluded from the final BOM and CPL files.\n\n[■] POINT 13: ANALOG RAIL ISOLATION (FB1 REMOVAL)\n    • Remove FB1 bridging +3.3V and +3.3VA between U2 and U3 outputs.\n    • Verify regulator outputs are physically and electrically separated \n      to guarantee clean analog rail integrity.\n\n[■] POINT 14: VMID_REFF BUFFER & QUIESCENT CURRENT REDUCTION\n    • Insert a low-quiescent-current voltage follower (buffer) between \n      the C34 midpoint and the VMID_REFF distribution node.\n    • Increase voltage divider resistor values (R43/R44) to reduce \n      continuous quiescent current consumption.\n\n[■] POINT 15: DESIGNATOR ALIGNMENT, LAYOUT & BOM CLEANUP\n    • PCB Layout: Ensure the 100 nF decoupling cap (C48) is physically \n      placed as close to U13 Pin 10 as practical.\n    • Documentation Sync: Update all notes and reports to reflect the \n      actual schematic designators: \n      - DS18B20 Pull-up: R61 (previously R19)\n      - LED Series Resistors: R59/R60 (previously R33/R36)\n      - INA333: U10 (previously U8)\n    • BOM Update: Correct J5/J6 descriptions from \n     \"LED_BLANK\" to \"LED_BANK\".\n    • Verify and update the stated standby current in \n      the final design notes."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 104.394 168.656 0)
